  "form": "Problem note",
  "pages": 16,
  "question": "Why is the sum over distinct running LCMs of the 5-smooth integers irrational?",
  "precis": "A five-map argument proves irrationality of the reciprocal sum over distinct running least common multiples of the 5-smooth integers. The spacing of powers of five separates the tail images, so rationality would force a periodic jump sequence. Counting running LCMs with multiplicity gives a different number, whose irrationality remains open here.",
  "owns": "the five-map proof for distinct running LCMs over {2,3,5}; the long paper treats general prime sets, the sum with multiplicity, kernels and residue criteria",
  "not_authority_for": "the validity of claims tagged Lean, which belongs to the cited kernel-checked source, or a solution to Erdős #269, which remains open",
